== Mock Examination 2 — Questions

#mcq(1, [A wave of period 0.050 s travels 60 m in 3.0 s. Its wavelength is], [0.50 m], [1.0 m], [2.0 m], [4.0 m])

#mcq(2, [A source of 600 Hz recedes from a stationary observer at 30 m s⁻¹. The observed frequency is ($v = 340$ m s⁻¹)], [551 Hz], [600 Hz], [654 Hz], [6000 Hz])

#mcq(3, [An object stands 20 cm in front of a convex mirror of focal length 15 cm. The image is], [8.6 cm behind the mirror], [8.6 cm in front of the mirror], [15 cm behind the mirror], [60 cm in front of the mirror])

#mcq(4, [The critical angle for a water-air boundary is ($n = 1.33$)], [42°], [49°], [60°], [90°])

#mcq(5, [An object 5.0 cm from a converging lens of focal length 10 cm gives an image that is], [real and 10 cm away], [virtual and 10 cm from the lens on the same side], [virtual and 5.0 cm away], [at infinity])

#mcq(6, [Which of these has the highest frequency?], [radio waves], [infrared], [visible light], [gamma rays])

#mcq(7, [A string 1.2 m long vibrates in four loops. The wavelength is], [0.30 m], [0.60 m], [1.2 m], [2.4 m])

#mcq(8, [A resonance tube resonates first at 17 cm and again at 51 cm. If the fork has a frequency of 500 Hz, the speed of sound is], [170 m s⁻¹], [255 m s⁻¹], [340 m s⁻¹], [500 m s⁻¹])

#mcq(9, [A ray strikes a plane mirror along the normal. The angle of reflection is], [0°], [45°], [90°], [180°])

#mcq(10, [The speed of light in diamond of refractive index 2.42 is about], [$1.2 times 10^8$ m s⁻¹], [$2.4 times 10^8$ m s⁻¹], [$3.0 times 10^8$ m s⁻¹], [$7.3 times 10^8$ m s⁻¹])

#mcq(11, [The image formed on the retina is], [virtual and upright], [real and inverted], [real and upright], [virtual and inverted])

#mcq(12, [Cyan, magenta and yellow are the primary colours of], [light], [the spectrum], [pigment], [photography only])

#mcq(13, [The speed of a wave on a string is doubled by multiplying the tension by], [2], [4], [$sqrt(2)$], [8])

#mcq(14, [The quality of a musical note is determined by its], [frequency], [amplitude], [speed], [overtones])

#mcq(15, [An object 10 cm from a concave mirror of focal length 15 cm gives an image that is], [real, 30 cm from the mirror], [real, 6.0 cm from the mirror], [virtual, 30 cm behind the mirror], [at infinity])

#mcq(16, [A glass block of refractive index 1.5 is 9.0 cm thick. An object seen through it appears raised by], [1.5 cm], [2.0 cm], [3.0 cm], [6.0 cm])

#mcq(17, [Two thin lenses of powers $+5.0$ D and $-2.0$ D are in contact. Their focal length is], [7.0 cm], [20 cm], [33 cm], [50 cm])

#mcq(18, [Which of these is *not* a member of the electromagnetic spectrum?], [radio waves], [sound waves], [ultraviolet], [gamma rays])

#mcq(19, [The distance from a node to the next antinode on a stationary wave is], [one wavelength], [half a wavelength], [a quarter of a wavelength], [two wavelengths])

#mcq(20, [The speed of sound in air at room temperature is about], [1500 m s⁻¹], [340 m s⁻¹], [30 m s⁻¹], [3.0 × 10⁸ m s⁻¹])

#mcq(21, [A concave mirror forms a real image whenever the object is], [at the focus], [inside the focus], [beyond the focus], [at the pole])

#mcq(22, [A ray in glass of refractive index 1.5 strikes the surface at 40°, the critical angle being 42°. The angle of refraction in the air is about], [42°], [60°], [75°], [90°])

#mcq(23, [The near point of a normal eye is about], [2.5 cm], [25 cm], [2.5 m], [infinity])

#mcq(24, [A lamp of intensity 100 cd is 5.0 m above a bench. The illuminance on the bench is], [4.0 lux], [20 lux], [100 lux], [500 lux])

#mcq(25, [A wave of frequency 2.5 kHz has a wavelength of 13.6 cm. Its speed is], [34 m s⁻¹], [136 m s⁻¹], [340 m s⁻¹], [3400 m s⁻¹])

#mcq(26, [An open pipe and a closed pipe have equal lengths. The ratio of their fundamental frequencies is], [2 : 1], [1 : 2], [1 : 1], [4 : 1])

#mcq(27, [The magnification produced by a plane mirror is], [0], [1], [2], [infinite])

#mcq(28, [A prism of angle 60° gives a deviation of 40° for a ray entering at 45°. The angle of emergence is], [25°], [45°], [55°], [85°])

#mcq(29, [The total magnification of a compound microscope is], [the sum of the two powers], [the difference of the two focal lengths], [the ratio of the two focal lengths], [the product of the two magnifications])

#mcq(30, [Diffraction of light is most marked when the size of the gap is], [much larger than the wavelength], [comparable with the wavelength], [much smaller than the wavelength], [irrelevant to the wavelength])

#mcq(31, [Three crests pass a point each second and the crests are 5.0 m apart. The speed is], [15 m s⁻¹], [5.0 m s⁻¹], [1.7 m s⁻¹], [0.60 m s⁻¹])

#mcq(32, [A source of 500 Hz recedes at 40 m s⁻¹. The observed frequency is ($v = 340$ m s⁻¹)], [447 Hz], [500 Hz], [559 Hz], [4470 Hz])

#mcq(33, [An object between F and C of a concave mirror forms an image that is], [at the focus, real and diminished], [at C, real and the same size], [behind the mirror, virtual and magnified], [beyond C, real and magnified])

#mcq(34, [Total internal reflection requires that light travels], [from a less dense to a denser medium at any angle], [from a denser to a less dense medium beyond the critical angle], [along the normal into a denser medium], [into a medium of the same refractive index])

#mcq(35, [A camera forms an image that is], [virtual and upright], [real and inverted], [real and upright], [virtual and inverted])

#mcq(36, [The polarisation of light shows that light], [is a particle stream], [is longitudinal], [is transverse], [needs a medium])

#mcq(37, [A wave of period 0.020 s has a wavelength of 4.0 m. Its speed is], [0.080 m s⁻¹], [0.50 m s⁻¹], [80 m s⁻¹], [200 m s⁻¹])

#mcq(38, [A sonar pulse returns from the sea bed after 0.40 s. If sound travels at 1500 m s⁻¹ in the water, the depth is], [150 m], [300 m], [600 m], [1200 m])

#mcq(39, [A reflecting telescope uses a concave mirror rather than a lens because a large mirror], [is cheaper], [gives an upright image], [collects more light without the weight and chromatic defect of a lens], [needs no adjustment])

#mcq(40, [In the spectrum produced by a prism, the colour nearest the original direction of the beam is], [red], [yellow], [green], [violet])

